# Job descriptions
job-description-canaan-abraham = Patriarch of Canaan. Keep the tent open on all four sides, greet every stranger with bread and water, and count the stars: your descendants will outnumber them.
job-description-canaan-isaac = Son of laughter and keeper of the wells. Re-dig your father's wells, sow the fields until they yield a hundredfold, and try your best to tell your sons apart.
job-description-canaan-jacob = Shepherd, dreamer, and part-time stew merchant. Tend the speckled flocks, dream of ladders, wrestle anyone who insists, and never trade a pot of lentil stew for less than a birthright.

# Supervisors
job-supervisors-canaan-abraham = the Almighty (and Sarah)
job-supervisors-canaan-isaac = your father Abraham
job-supervisors-canaan-jacob = your father Isaac (and your mother Rebekah, who has a plan)

# Lobby
canaan-lobby-subtext = Where the tent flaps are always open.
canaan-lobby-description = A slice of the Holy Land adrift in the Frontier sector, complete with desert sand, palms, and a working well. Here you can:
   - Break bread with the household of Abraham
   - Draw water from the well of Beersheba and work the fields of Gerar
   - Tend goats, sleep under the stars at Bethel, and guard the lentil stew
 {"["}color=gray]Each patriarch is a single slot. First come, first blessed.[/color]

